  "methodology": "Land FMV is built bottoms-up by grouping LAND's ~99K acres into eight crop / region buckets and applying a per-acre value sourced from the USDA NASS 2024 Land Values Summary, recent third-party appraisals (where the company has disclosed them in past investor materials), and comparable transactions reported by the regional ag-real-estate brokers cited above. Buckets are then aggregated to a portfolio FMV. Implied NAV/share at FMV deducts net debt (long-term debt + Series D Term Pref − cash) and divides by current diluted shares outstanding. The result is a sum-of-the-parts estimate, not a single appraisal — California permanent and coastal ground drives the bulk of the gap to book, since LAND acquired most of those farms 5–10 years ago at materially lower per-acre values."
